   "author": "Jack",
   "date": "2025-02-20T08:09:25",
   "content_html": "<p>Brilliant post!  I drank their Kool-Aid, paid for an annual subscription, and regretted it after the first 2 hours trying to learn their app. </p>\n<p>Several times I asked CoachCat for a more detailed analysis of my rides beyond the general &#8220;cheerleading&#8221; post ride responses (example 1, to summarize my average torque for each of their low cadence intervals and example 2, to summarize my average power for each interval completed). The CoachCat response I received was along the lines of &#8220;I can&#8217;t provide a summary of this data as I can&#8217;t analyze the uploaded .fit file. If you can provide me more details by looking at your file, that would help me interpret them. Alternatively, you can use software that reads .fit files to view your data&#8221;. Essentially, I would have to do the analysis myself and report the details back to CoachCat&#8230;</p>\n<p>You are correct, it is a slick app with slick marketing.  It does have a ton of pre-made programs to choose from that I can at least look through and learn potentially new ideas.</p>\n"
  }
 ],
